Z||000000||Zoom88||12-15-2001||10:43 AM|||| I read all the post on plug wires and majority suggested Accel, I decided on the 8.8 (8879, custom fitpart number)Thanks everyone  for the vast info. one can always find on this Forum !!! <BR> Here are some pics for anyone interested, this is my 88 Formula 120,000 mile and still kickin !!!<BR> PS.  Just installed the wires this morning...I love them wires !!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-551f.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-553f.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-554f.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-555f.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-556f.jpg"> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||12-15-2001||11:05 AM||||Lookin good!<P>Make sure you post one of those pictures in the clean engine compartment thread if you haven't already!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerwinter3.gif">           <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.envy.nu/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||14
Z||000002||recluse||12-15-2001||11:47 AM||||Looks good, and clean too.  I dont know about the Accel 8.8's but Ive had 2 pairs of the 8mm wires and they where junk.  They made the car miss under a load.  I have Magnecor wires now, I like them alot.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||12-15-2001||12:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR><B>I dont know about the Accel 8.8's but Ive had 2 pairs of the 8mm wires and they where junk.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well it's a little late now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>That is one clean engine compartment!||||reg||1
Z||000004||California Kid||12-15-2001||12:38 PM||||Great looking engine compartment!!!<P>It appears the boots at the spark plugs are too long, did they come that way, or are they not seated fully into the metal shields?||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||12-15-2001||05:46 PM||||Has the recall ever been done on this car?  The forward engine deck lid wipe strip was removed as a suspected contributor to engine fires.  You seem to have a brand new one here.<P>Of course, many edge wipers have been re-installed in the susbsequent years.  I believe that there is even a new stainless steel version available from your neck of the woods.||||reg||5
Z||000006||REDHOTT88||12-15-2001||06:27 PM||||That engine is just.....BEAUTIFUL!<P>I think I'm going to cry. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">      <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Zoom88||12-15-2001||10:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Great looking engine compartment!!!<P>It appears the boots at the spark plugs are too long, did they come that way, or are they not seated fully into the metal shields?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Good eye, I had just put them on . Had them just sittin on the plugs.  I was debating on wheather or not to change out the plugs even though they where low mileage. Decided to do it, but wanted to get some pics before I got off into it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||12-16-2001||04:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR><B>Looks good, and clean too.  I dont know about the Accel 8.8's but Ive had 2 pairs of the 8mm wires and they where junk.  They made the car miss under a load.  I have Magnecor wires now, I like them alot.  Good luck.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 8mm Accel wires (so called super stock)<BR>are junk but the 8.8s arent! I've had two friends use the regular super stock ones and their old wires actually performed better!<BR>The 8.8 wires are excellent though and I think you'll be very happy with them for a very long time!! I have used the 8.8's for years on many different cars and have had many friends switch to them after seeing my results with them.<BR>That engine is very clean and it looks great!!!<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>Activities Director<BR>Northern IL. Fiero Enthusiasts<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000009||Zoom88||12-16-2001||09:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B> The 8mm Accel wires (so called super stock)<BR>are junk but the 8.8s arent! I've had two friends use the regular super stock ones and their old wires actually performed better!<BR>The 8.8 wires are excellent though and I think you'll be very happy with them for a very long time!! I have used the 8.8's for years on many different cars and have had many friends switch to them after seeing my results with them.<BR>That engine is very clean and it looks great!!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Thanks for all the positive responses, it makes all the hard work worth it !!! I have noticed my idle has become somewhat better. Could be my old wires were just going bad.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jake_Dragon||12-16-2001||03:01 PM||||Sweet, I want some.<BR>Santa you listing? I've been good honest.<P>I purchased my GT and the wires were all burnt. I could not beleve the difference when I put new ones on.<P>Wating on spring to do a tune up and looks like I know what wires to get.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon14.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||14
